{"id":"mahabharata-2-020","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":20,"title":"विंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 20 · Krishna challenges Jarasandha","summary":{"en":"Jarasandha asks what wrong he has done them. Krishna reveals who they are and rebukes him for imprisoning kings to sacrifice them to Shiva, an act that dishonours all kshatriyas, and challenges him to fight one of them; Jarasandha chooses Bhima.","kn":"ತಾನು ಅವರಿಗೆ ಏನು ತಪ್ಪು ಮಾಡಿದೆ ಎಂದು ಜರಾಸಂಧನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ತಾವು ಯಾರೆಂದು ತಿಳಿಸಿ, ಶಿವನಿಗೆ ಬಲಿಕೊಡಲು ರಾಜರನ್ನು ಸೆರೆಹಿಡಿದು ಎಲ್ಲ ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯರಿಗೆ ಅವಮಾನ ಮಾಡಿದ್ದಕ್ಕೆ ಗದರಿಸಿ, ತಮ್ಮಲ್ಲಿ ಒಬ್ಬನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಯುದ್ಧಕ್ಕೆ ಆಹ್ವಾನಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಜರಾಸಂಧನು ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಆರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"जरासन्ध पूछता है कि उसने उनका क्या अपराध किया है। श्रीकृष्ण अपना परिचय देकर उसे शिव को बलि देने के लिए राजाओं को बन्दी बनाने के लिए फटकारते हैं, जो सब क्षत्रियों का अपमान है, और उनमें से किसी एक से युद्ध की चुनौती देते हैं; जरासन्ध भीम को चुनता है।","te":"తాను వారికి ఏ అపకారం చేశానని జరాసంధుడు అడుగుతాడు. శ్రీకృష్ణుడు తామెవరో తెలిపి, శివునికి బలి ఇవ్వడానికి రాజులను బంధించి క్షత్రియులందరినీ అవమానించినందుకు మందలించి, తమలో ఒకరితో యుద్ధానికి సవాలు చేస్తాడు; జరాసంధుడు భీముని ఎంచుకుంటాడు.","ta":"தான் அவர்களுக்கு என்ன தீங்கு செய்தேன் என்று ஜராஸந்தன் கேட்கிறான். ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் தாம் யாரென்று வெளிப்படுத்தி, ஶிவனுக்குப் பலியிட மன்னர்களைச் சிறைப்படுத்தி எல்லா க்ஷத்ரியர்களையும் இழிவுபடுத்தியதற்காகக் கடிந்து, தம்மில் ஒருவருடன் போரிட அழைக்கிறார்; ஜராஸந்தன் பீமனைத் தேர்ந்தெடுக்கிறான்.","ml":"തങ്ങളോട് താൻ എന്ത് തെറ്റാണ് ചെയ്തതെന്ന് ജരാസന്ധൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. കൃഷ്ണൻ തങ്ങളാരാണെന്ന് വെളിപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു; രാജാക്കന്മാരെ തടവിലാക്കി ശിവന് ബലി നൽകുന്നത് സകല ക്ഷത്രിയരെയും അപമാനിക്കുന്ന പ്രവൃത്തിയാണെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം ശാസിക്കുന്നു; അവരിലൊരാളോട് യുദ്ധം ചെയ്യാൻ വെല്ലുവിളിക്കുന്നു. ജരാസന്ധൻ ഭീമനെ തിരഞ്ഞെടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.20; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"जरासंधवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jarasandhavadha Parva (Slaying of Jarasandha)","verses":[{"text":"जरासंध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Jarasandha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"न स्मरेयं कदा वैरं कृतं युष्माभिरित्युत ।\nचिन्तयंश्च न पश्यामि भवतां प्रति वैकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not remember ever doing you any enmity; though I think hard, I see no wrong done by me against you."}},{"n":2,"text":"वैकृते चासति कथं मन्यध्वं मामनागसम् ।\nअरिं विब्रूत तद्विप्राः सतां समय एष हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"When no wrong has been done, Brahmins, how do you treat me, who have done nothing wrong, as an enemy? Tell me; this is the way of good men."}},{"n":3,"text":"अथ धर्मोपघाताद्धि मनः समुपतप्यते ।\nयोऽनागसि प्रसृजति क्षत्रियोऽपि न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the mind is tormented by a breach of dharma; one who harms the innocent, even a Kshatriya, surely suffers."}},{"n":4,"text":"अतोऽन्यथाचरँल्लोके धर्मज्ञः सन्महाव्रतः ।\nवृजिनां गतिमाप्नोति श्रेयसोऽप्युपहन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who acts otherwise in the world, though he knows dharma and keeps great vows, reaches the state of sinners and loses what is better."}},{"n":5,"text":"त्रैलोक्ये क्षत्रधर्माद्धि श्रेयांसं साधुचारिणाम् ।\nअनागसं प्रजानानाः प्रमादादिव जल्पथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the three worlds there is nothing better, for those who live well, than the dharma of the Kshatriya; yet you speak as though by oversight, knowing me innocent."}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"कुलकार्यं महाराज कश्चिदेकः कुलोद्वहः ।\nवहते तन्नियोगाद्वै वयमभ्युत्थितास्त्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, some one man who supports the family carries out the family's task; by his command we three have risen up."}},{"n":7,"text":"त्वया चोपहृता राजन्क्षत्रिया लोकवासिनः ।\nतदागः क्रूरमुत्पाद्य मन्यसे किं त्वनागसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have taken captive the Kshatriyas who live in the world; having committed that cruel wrong, do you think yourself innocent?"}},{"n":8,"text":"राजा राज्ञः कथं साधून्हिंस्यान्नृपतिसत्तम ।\nतद्राज्ञः संनिगृह्य त्वं रुद्रायोपजिहीर्षसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of kings, how can a king harm good kings? Having seized those kings, you wish to offer them to Rudra."}},{"n":9,"text":"अस्मांस्तदेनो गच्छेत त्वया बार्हद्रथे कृतम् ।\nवयं हि शक्ता धर्मस्य रक्षणे धर्मचारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That sin which you, son of Brihadratha, have committed would come upon us; for we, who follow dharma, are able to protect it."}},{"n":10,"text":"मनुष्याणां समालम्भो न च दृष्टः कदाचन ।\nस कथं मानुषैर्देवं यष्टुमिच्छसि शंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sacrifice of men has never been seen; how then do you wish to worship the god Shankara with men?"}},{"n":11,"text":"सवर्णो हि सवर्णानां पशुसंज्ञां करिष्यति ।\nकोऽन्य एवं यथा हि त्वं जरासंध वृथामतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One of the same class will call his own class \"animals\"; who but you, Jarasandha, of foolish mind, would do so?"}},{"n":12,"text":"ते त्वां ज्ञातिक्षयकरं वयमार्तानुसारिणः ।\nज्ञातिवृद्धिनिमित्तार्थं विनियन्तुमिहागताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We, who go to help the afflicted, have come here to restrain you, destroyer of your kin, for the sake of increasing our kin."}},{"n":13,"text":"नास्ति लोके पुमानन्यः क्षत्रियेष्विति चैव यत् ।\nमन्यसे स च ते राजन्सुमहान्बुद्धिविप्लवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And your thought that there is no other man among the Kshatriyas is a great confusion of mind."}},{"n":14,"text":"को हि जानन्नभिजनमात्मनः क्षत्रियो नृप ।\nनाविशेत्स्वर्गमतुलं रणानन्तरमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What Kshatriya, knowing his own lineage, would not enter after battle the incomparable, undying heaven?"}},{"n":15,"text":"स्वर्गं ह्येव समास्थाय रणयज्ञेषु दीक्षिताः ।\nयजन्ते क्षत्रिया लोकांस्तद्विद्धि मगधाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fixing their aim on heaven, consecrated in the sacrifices of war, Kshatriyas win the worlds; know this, lord of Magadha."}},{"n":16,"text":"स्वर्गयोनिर्जयो राजन्स्वर्गयोनिर्महद्यशः ।\nस्वर्गयोनिस्तपो युद्धे मार्गः सोऽव्यभिचारवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victory, great fame and austerity in battle are the sources of heaven; that path never fails."}},{"n":17,"text":"एष ह्यैन्द्रो वैजयन्तो गुणो नित्यं समाहितः ।\nयेनासुरान्पराजित्य जगत्पाति शतक्रतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is Indra's Vaijayanta quality, always kept ready, by which Shatakratu defeats the Asuras and protects the world."}},{"n":18,"text":"स्वर्गमास्थाय कस्य स्याद्विग्रहित्वं यथा तव ।\nमागधैर्विपुलैः सैन्यैर्बाहुल्यबलदर्पितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who that has set his mind on heaven would be a fighter like you, with vast Magadha armies, proud of their number and strength?"}},{"n":19,"text":"मावमंस्थाः परान्राजन्नास्ति वीर्यं नरे नरे ।\nसमं तेजस्त्वया चैव केवलं मनुजेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not despise others, king; there is no special valor in one man or another; the same fire is in them as in you, O lord of men."}},{"n":20,"text":"यावदेव न संबुद्धं तावदेव भवेत्तव ।\nविषह्यमेतदस्माकमतो राजन्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Only so long as this is not understood will it be as you think; we can withstand this, and so I tell you, king."}},{"n":21,"text":"जहि त्वं सदृशेष्वेव मानं दर्पं च मागध ।\nमा गमः ससुतामात्यः सबलश्च यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give up your pride and arrogance toward your equals, lord of Magadha; do not go to Yama's house with your sons, ministers and army."}},{"n":22,"text":"दम्भोद्भवः कार्तवीर्य उत्तरश्च बृहद्रथः ।\nश्रेयसो ह्यवमन्येह विनेशुः सबला नृपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dambhodbhava, Kartavirya, Uttara and Brihadratha, and kings with their armies, perished here by despising those better than themselves."}},{"n":23,"text":"मुमुक्षमाणास्त्वत्तश्च न वयं ब्राह्मणब्रुवाः ।\nशौरिरस्मि हृषीकेशो नृवीरौ पाण्डवाविमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"We are not mere Brahmin pretenders, wishing to free the kings from you; I am Shauri, Hrishikesha, and these two are the Pandavas, heroes among men."}},{"n":24,"text":"त्वामाह्वयामहे राजन्स्थिरो युध्यस्व मागध ।\nमुञ्च वा नृपतीन्सर्वान्मा गमस्त्वं यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We call you out, king: stand firm and fight, lord of Magadha, or free all the kings; do not go to Yama's abode."}},{"text":"जरासंध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Jarasandha said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"नाजितान्वै नरपतीनहमादद्मि कांश्चन ।\nजितः कः पर्यवस्थाता कोऽत्र यो न मया जितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I take no kings who are not conquered; who, once conquered, remains standing here? Who is there that I have not conquered?"}},{"n":26,"text":"क्षत्रियस्यैतदेवाहुर्धर्म्यं कृष्णोपजीवनम् ।\nविक्रम्य वशमानीय कामतो यत्समाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, they say this is a Kshatriya's dharma: to live by valor, bringing others under his control and doing what he wishes."}},{"n":27,"text":"देवतार्थमुपाकृत्य राज्ञः कृष्ण कथं भयात् ।\nअहमद्य विमुञ्चेयं क्षात्रं व्रतमनुस्मरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having set kings aside for the gods, Krishna, how could I let them go out of fear, remembering the Kshatriya's vow?"}},{"n":28,"text":"सैन्यं सैन्येन व्यूढेन एक एकेन वा पुनः ।\nद्वाभ्यां त्रिभिर्वा योत्स्येऽहं युगपत्पृथगेव वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will fight army with army in array, or one against one, or against two or three, together or one at a time."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा जरासंधः सहदेवाभिषेचनम् ।\nआज्ञापयत्तदा राजा युयुत्सुर्भीमकर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, Jarasandha, eager for fighting with dread deeds, ordered the consecration of Sahadeva."}},{"n":30,"text":"स तु सेनापती राजा सस्मार भरतर्षभ ।\nकौशिकं चित्रसेनं च तस्मिन्युद्ध उपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"O bull of the Bharatas, when the battle was at hand, the king remembered his commanders Kaushika and Chitrasena,"}},{"n":31,"text":"ययोस्ते नामनी लोके हंसेति डिभकेति च ।\nपूर्वं संकथिते पुम्भिर्नृलोके लोकसत्कृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"whose names in the world are Hamsa and Dibhaka, as men have earlier recounted in the world of men honored by all."}},{"n":32,"text":"तं तु राजन्विभुः शौरी राजानं बलिनां वरम् ।\nस्मृत्वा पुरुषशार्दूल शार्दूलसमविक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, the lord Shauri, remembering that king, best of the mighty, with tiger-like valor,"}},{"n":33,"text":"सत्यसंधो जरासंधं भुवि भीमपराक्रमम् ।\nभागमन्यस्य निर्दिष्टं वध्यं भूमिभृदच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"true to his word, knew that Jarasandha, fierce in valor on earth, supporter of the earth, was another's portion to kill."}},{"n":34,"text":"नात्मनात्मवतां मुख्य इयेष मधुसूदनः ।\nब्रह्मणोऽऽज्ञां पुरस्कृत्य हन्तुं हलधरानुजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, best of the self-possessed, honoring Brahma's command, did not wish to kill him himself, though he was the younger brother of the plowman Balarama."}}]}]}